* "German Quad", channel 2: V1A, GAIN 2 and the tube M1, V2A and the V2B follower, the CH2 tone stack and VOLUME 2. See preamp.net for the drawing and the assumptions.

V VRAIL x 100 400
R R86 x dp 8.2k
C C87 dp 0 19u
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

* V1A: 1M and 100p to ground, the 68k stopper (the input capacitor is bridged on the drawing), 1k2 with 10u on the cathode, 120k plate load.
R R1M in 0 1M
C C100P in 0 100p
R R68K in g1 68k
T V1A g1 p1 k1 12AX7
R R1K2 k1 0 1.2k
C C10U k1 0 10u
R R120A dp p1 120k

* CH2: 22n, 2M2 with 68p across into the node n1 (220k to ground), GAIN 2 (220k-A wiper pot) with 220k at its wiper, the gain tube M1 (120k plate, 680R with 1u), 4n7,
* 470k (the BRIGHT switch puts 470p across it) to h with 470k to ground.
C C22N p1 m 22n
R R2M2 m n1 2.2M
C C68P m n1 68p
R R220N n1 0 220k
R VRG_T n1 g2 1
R VRG_B g2 0 1
R R220G g2 0 220k
T M1 g2 pm1 km1 12AX7
R R120M dp pm1 120k
R R680M km1 0 680
C C1UM km1 0 1u
C C4N7M pm1 q 4.7n
R R470Q q h 470k
C C470P q br2 470p
R SW_BR2 br2 h 1e12
R R470R h 0 470k

* The input of the next stage (R470H 470k into V2A's grid and its input capacitance, about 110 pF), repeated here so the cut at h keeps its load; the rail
* resistor above is scaled by (the channel's current / this stage's current) so the plates sit where they did in one netlist.
R RDUM h hd 470k
C CDUM hd 0 110p
